---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { VIDEO_BASE } from "../videoBase";

// Static page — generated at build time, not per request. Webflow Cloud
// requires output: "server". These pages were prerendered (`= true`); the
// Basic-auth gate in src/middleware.ts only runs for on-demand routes, so they
// are server-rendered instead. Flip back to `true` and delete the middleware to
// restore static generation.
export const prerender = false;
---

<Base title="Communications — Saltenna" description="Saltenna Plasmonix™ communications: high-bandwidth, stealthy wireless links underwater, through ice, through metal, underground, and in dense vegetation" active="communications">

  <section class="page-hero color-media sea-hero">
    <video class="bg-video" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto" poster="images/posters/comms-hero-fleet.jpg" aria-hidden="true">
      <source src={`${VIDEO_BASE}/comms-hero-fleet.mp4`} type="video/mp4" />
    </video>
    <div class="container hero-lead">
      <h1>Communications where wireless can't reach</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="container hero-info">
      <div class="hero-info-tag">
        <p>Beyond legacy radio frequency</p>
        <a class="hero-scroll" href="#use-cases" aria-label="Scroll to content">&#8595;</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-info-desc">Saltenna is developing high-bandwidth communications underwater, under ice, through dense infrastructure, and beyond — across government and commercial sectors</p>
      <nav class="hero-info-links" aria-label="Communications use cases">
        <a href="#uc-water">Water &amp; Ice</a>
        <a href="#uc-metal">Steel &amp; Concrete</a>
        <a href="#uc-surfaces">Surfaces</a>
        <a href="#uc-pipes">Pipes</a>
        <a href="#uc-beyond">Beyond</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block deep has-fx" id="use-cases">
    <canvas class="fx-canvas" data-fx="sonar" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2>Five barriers. One physics.</h2>
        <p>Plasmonix™ waves travel along the boundaries other signals can't cross. If an environment defeats today's wireless, it's a candidate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="split use-case-panel reveal" id="uc-water">
        <div>
          <h3>Through Water and Ice</h3>
          <p>Saltenna is developing high-bandwidth, stealthy communications underwater — no line of sight required — and through and along ice sheets, connecting air and above-ice assets with those submerged beneath</p>
        </div>
        <div class="split-media scene" data-parallax="0.22">
          <img src="images/uc/comms-underwater.svg?v=2" alt="" loading="lazy">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="split reverse use-case-panel reveal" id="uc-metal">
        <div>
          <h3>Through Steel and Concrete</h3>
          <p>Saltenna has demonstrated significantly enhanced range in solid underground facilities, tunnels, and multi-level structures, and is working on robust links inside ships, submarines, and dense or collapsed infrastructure — with no cables run and no holes drilled</p>
        </div>
        <div class="split-media scene" data-parallax="0.22">
          <img src="images/uc/comms-ships.svg?v=2" alt="" loading="lazy">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="split use-case-panel reveal" id="uc-surfaces">
        <div>
          <h3>Along Surfaces</h3>
          <p>Any long conductive surface can become the network. Saltenna is developing stealthy, resilient communications along linear infrastructure — runways, flightlines, roads — and around metal airframes themselves, with signals riding the surface instead of broadcasting into contested spectrum.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="split-media scene" data-parallax="0.22">
          <img src="images/uc/comms-runways.svg?v=2" alt="" loading="lazy">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="split reverse use-case-panel reveal" id="uc-pipes">
        <div>
          <h3>Along Pipes and Industrial Metal</h3>
          <p>Saltenna has demonstrated wireless communications along and through pressurized tanks and pipes, and is working on links for pipelines above ground, buried, or underwater — including lines filled with hazardous liquids — without drilling holes or running wires</p>
        </div>
        <div class="split-media scene" data-parallax="0.22">
          <img src="images/uc/comms-pipelines.svg?v=2" alt="" loading="lazy">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="split use-case-panel reveal" id="uc-beyond">
        <div>
          <h3>Where Nothing Else Reaches</h3>
          <p>Where there are no towers and no ionosphere, the physics still holds. Saltenna is working on carrying communications within and through dense jungle canopy, and simulations show the technology could work on the lunar surface and other planets.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="split-media scene" data-parallax="0.22">
          <img src="images/uc/comms-jungle-canopy.svg?v=2" alt="" loading="lazy">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block dark has-fx">
    <canvas class="fx-canvas" data-fx="field" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split reveal">
        <div class="split-media graphic">
          <iframe src="graphics/saltenna-vs-conventional.html" title="Interactive 3D: conventional RF radiating and blocked by a barrier, beside a Plasmonix™ packet that follows the metal surface to the far node" loading="lazy"></iframe>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>A technology that behaves differently from all others</h3>
          <p>Current radios, Wi‑Fi, Bluetooth, optical, audio, and other systems radiate through free space and fail at dense obstacles. Plasmonix™ waves instead travel along surfaces — the boundaries between water, metal, soil, and air — so no line of sight is needed, and the energy stays stealthy on the surface instead of broadcasting into contested spectrum.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band has-fx">
    <canvas class="fx-canvas" data-fx="field" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="container reveal">
      <h2>Saltenna is evolving fast</h2>
      <p>We are developing seemingly impossible communications and sensing at the edge in the most demanding environments. Contact us to explore and craft powerful unique solutions.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="contact.html">Contact Us</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
